  "notes": "ENTERABLE. Round tapered plaster tower (8 m base -> 6.4 m at 21 m), 6 storeys of 3.4 m (floors at z 0.2/3.6/7.0/10.4/13.8/17.2), flat roof with a projecting gallery band at 20.3 m, and a 6 m round lantern drum rising through the roof to 24.6 m under a conical metal cap (tip ~26.8 m). Single timber door on the s face, centre 0, 1.1 x 2.1 m, sill 0. Stair is AUTHORED (the auto-siter could not fit a 4.6 m flight in the narrowing round plan and fell back to the axis, with alternate flights poking through the upper walls): five flights of 16 risers x 0.2125 m (tread 0.24, run 3.84 m, width 0.95), runs along y from y +1.9 (foot, 1.6 m inside the door) to y -1.9, climbing away from the door; flights alternate between x +0.625 (flights 1,3,5) and x -0.625 (2,4) so both stay >= 0.4 m inside the wall at the top storey. Every storey reached (floors_built 6 = declared 6). The top storey opens upward into the lantern drum (glazing 21.7-23.5 m, four faces) so the lamp room is visible from the top landing. Small windows alternate s/e (floors 2,4,6) and n/w (floors 3,5). Lantern is 'round' not octagonal because Mason's polygon puts vertices on the axes (every window would land on a corner). Round plan -> ~8.6k collision-shell tris: accepted for the one landmark, per mason.md."
 },
